{
  "name": "workboard",
  "version": "0.0.0",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js",
    "test": "node --test"
  }
}
# Workboard

Requires Node.js 22.22.1. No external dependencies or installation are needed.

```sh
npm start
```

The server binds to `0.0.0.0:8080`. Configure the port and persistent SQLite file with:

```sh
PORT=8080 DB_PATH=./data/workboard.sqlite npm start
```

Open `/` to create and open projects. `GET /health` returns `{"status":"ok"}`.

Each project page lets you create tasks, toggle their completion, and filter by
All, Open, Completed, or Deleted. A separate Priority filter offers All, Low, Normal, and
High. Tasks must match both filters and retain their creation order. Task edits
preserve both selections and immediately update the matching rows. Both filters
remain usable in archived projects, and completion summaries always count all live
tasks. The project list shows completion summaries and lets you
filter Active or Archived projects, archive projects, and restore them. Archived
projects keep their tasks visible but disable task creation and completion changes.
Active project pages also let you rename projects with `New project name` and
`Rename project`. Names are trimmed and required. Renaming preserves the URL,
creation order, tasks, and completion summary. Archived projects disable renaming;
restoration enables it again.
Each task can also be renamed and assigned a Low, Normal, or High priority.
Existing tasks default to Normal. Each project's Default task priority starts at
Normal and can be set to Low, Normal, or High. New tasks inherit the saved default;
changing it leaves existing tasks and both filters unchanged. Defaults persist
independently for each project and are disabled during archival.
Renaming preserves completion and
priority; archived projects disable task renaming and priority changes.
Each task also has an optional Task due date and Save due date button. Dates use
real Gregorian calendar days in YYYY-MM-DD format (years 0001–9999), without
timezone conversion. Saving blank text clears the date; invalid dates show an
alert and preserve the saved value. Due dates persist independently, and archived
projects disable their date controls until restoration.
Project pages also provide Due from and Due through fields and Apply due range.
Applied boundaries are inclusive and intersect the completion and priority filters.
Either boundary can be blank; undated tasks match only when both are blank.
Invalid dates or reversed boundaries show an alert and preserve the applied range.
Task edits immediately update matching rows without resetting any filter. Range
controls remain usable while archived, and opening a project starts with empty
boundaries.
Each task row offers Destination project and Move task. Destinations list other
active projects in project creation order. A first arrival appends the task after all
positions established in its destination; returning restores its remembered position.
Positions are remembered independently per project and survive restarts. Moving
preserves its identity, title, completion, priority and due date, and keeps the source
page and all filters open. Summaries reflect current ownership. Archived projects
cannot send or receive tasks; move controls are disabled when archived or when no
eligible destination exists.
Projects, names, tasks, and archive state persist in the configured SQLite file; existing
databases are migrated automatically.

The project list provides Project search and Search projects. Each project page
provides Task search and Search tasks. Search applies a substring query with ASCII
case ignored and surrounding query whitespace trimmed. Runs of ASCII spaces and
horizontal tabs in queries and names/titles match as one space, without changing
the saved or displayed names/titles. Other internal whitespace remains significant.
Project search intersects Active/Archived, and task search intersects completion,
priority, and the applied due range. Searches retain all other filters, order, and
all-live-task summaries. Edits immediately update task search membership. Search remains
usable while archived and starts empty when opening either page or returning through
Projects.

Run the integration checks with `npm test`.

Each task row provides a multiline Task notes field and Save notes button. Notes
are saved as plain text exactly as entered, including whitespace, Unicode and
literal markup; empty text clears them. Notes persist and travel with moved tasks
without changing any other data or filters. Searches still match only names and
titles. Archived projects display notes with editing disabled until restoration.
Existing databases initialize notes to empty while preserving all prior data.

Live task rows offer Delete task; deleted rows offer Restore task. Deletion is
persistent and reversible, retaining all fields and remembered project positions.
All, Open and Completed exclude deleted tasks; Deleted intersects the same priority,
due range and title search controls. Summaries count only live tasks. Deleted rows
show saved data with editing and movement disabled until restoration. Archived
projects also disable deletion and restoration. Database upgrades keep existing
tasks live.

Every project page offers Download project, including archived projects. It downloads
UTF-8 JSON as `workboard-project.json` with format `workboard-project`, version 1,
and the current project name, archive state, default priority, and all live and
deleted tasks in stored order. Exports include task title, completion, priority,
due date, notes and deletion state, independently of page filters. Notes line
breaks use LF in the portable document; exporting leaves saved data and page
controls unchanged.

The home page provides Project JSON, Imported project name and Import project.
Paste a version 1 portable document and enter a nonblank override name to create
and open a new independent project. The complete document is validated before a
single transaction creates the project and its tasks. Invalid documents and blank
names show an alert, retain the submitted fields, and leave existing data unchanged.
Imports preserve task order, exact titles, completion, explicit priorities, due
dates, notes (with LF line endings), deletion status, project archival and default
priority. Imported copies receive new identities and remembered ordering positions;
editing or restoring a copy never changes the original.

The home page's Task directory opens `/task-directory`, a directory across
projects. Project scope (Active/Archived), Task filter, Priority filter, inclusive
due range and title-only Directory search intersect without changing saved data.
Each opening resets the controls to Active, All, All and empty range/search.
Results follow project creation order and each owner's stored task order, with
literal titles, owner names, completion, priority, due dates and multiline notes.
Deleted tasks appear only under Deleted. Open project navigates to the owner with
the usual project-page defaults; Projects returns home. Directory rows have no
editing controls, including for archived or deleted tasks.

Complete visible tasks and Reopen visible tasks update completion for the current
intersection across active projects, retaining every filter, search and applied
range. Changes are saved atomically and preserve all other fields and remembered
positions. Archived scope and Deleted disable both actions; each action is also
disabled when no matching live task needs that change. Summaries reflect the saved
completion state. Empty resolved results show No matching tasks; this announcement
stays hidden while directory results are loading or a bulk update is pending.
const app = document.querySelector('#app');

function asciiLower(value) {
  return value.replace(/[A-Z]/g, (letter) => letter.toLowerCase());
}

function matchesSearch(value, query) {
  return asciiLower(value.replace(/[ \t]+/g, ' '))
    .includes(asciiLower(query.replace(/[ \t]+/g, ' ')));
}

async function request(path, options) {
  const response = await fetch(path, options);
  const body = await response.json();
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(body.error || 'Unable to complete request');
  return body;
}

function showError(error) {
  let alert = app.querySelector('[role="alert"]');
  if (!alert) {
    alert = document.createElement('p');
    alert.setAttribute('role', 'alert');
    app.append(alert);
  }
  alert.textContent = error.message;
}

function validRangeDate(value) {
  if (value === '') return true;
  if (!/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/.test(value)) return false;
  const [year, month, day] = value.split('-').map(Number);
  if (year < 1 || month < 1 || month > 12) return false;
  const leap = year % 4 === 0 && (year % 100 !== 0 || year % 400 === 0);
  const days = [31, leap ? 29 : 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31];
  return day >= 1 && day <= days[month - 1];
}

function matchesTask(task, completion, priority, from, through, query) {
  return matchesSearch(task.title, query) &&
    (completion === 'deleted' ? task.deleted : !task.deleted &&
      (completion === 'all' || (completion === 'completed' ? task.completed : !task.completed))) &&
    (priority === 'all' || task.priority === priority) &&
    ((!from && !through) || (task.due_date !== '' &&
      (!from || task.due_date >= from) && (!through || task.due_date <= through)));
}

async function renderDirectory() {
  document.title = 'Task directory · Workboard';
  app.innerHTML = `
    <button type="button" id="back">Projects</button>
    <h1>Task directory</h1>
    <label for="project-scope">Project scope</label>
    <select id="project-scope">
      <option value="active">Active</option>
      <option value="archived">Archived</option>
    </select>
    <label for="task-filter">Task filter</label>
    <select id="task-filter">
      <option value="all">All</option>
      <option value="open">Open</option>
      <option value="completed">Completed</option>
      <option value="deleted">Deleted</option>
    </select>
    <label for="priority-filter">Priority filter</label>
    <select id="priority-filter">
      <option value="all">All</option>
      <option value="Low">Low</option>
      <option value="Normal">Normal</option>
      <option value="High">High</option>
    </select>
    <form id="directory-search-form">
      <label for="directory-search">Directory search</label>
      <input id="directory-search" type="text" autocomplete="off">
      <button type="submit">Search directory</button>
    </form>
    <form id="due-range">
      <label for="due-from">Due from</label>
      <input id="due-from" type="text" autocomplete="off">
      <label for="due-through">Due through</label>
      <input id="due-through" type="text" autocomplete="off">
      <button type="submit">Apply due range</button>
    </form>
    <button type="button" id="complete-visible" disabled>Complete visible tasks</button>
    <button type="button" id="reopen-visible" disabled>Reopen visible tasks</button>
    <p id="empty-directory" role="status" hidden>No matching tasks</p>
    <ul id="directory-tasks" aria-label="Task directory"></ul>`;
  app.querySelector('#back').addEventListener('click', () => { window.location.href = '/'; });
  const scope = app.querySelector('#project-scope');
  const completion = app.querySelector('#task-filter');
  const priority = app.querySelector('#priority-filter');
  const search = app.querySelector('#directory-search');
  const from = app.querySelector('#due-from');
  const through = app.querySelector('#due-through');
  const list = app.querySelector('#directory-tasks');
  const complete = app.querySelector('#complete-visible');
  const reopen = app.querySelector('#reopen-visible');
  let query = '';
  let appliedFrom = '';
  let appliedThrough = '';
  let tasks = [];
  let loading = true;
  let resolved = false;
  function draw() {
    list.replaceChildren();
    const visible = tasks.filter((task) => task.archived === (scope.value === 'archived') &&
      matchesTask(task, completion.value, priority.value, appliedFrom, appliedThrough, query));
    app.querySelector('#empty-directory').hidden = loading || !resolved || visible.length > 0;
    list.setAttribute('aria-busy', String(loading));
    const readOnly = loading || scope.value === 'archived' || completion.value === 'deleted';
    complete.disabled = readOnly || !visible.some((task) => !task.completed);
    reopen.disabled = readOnly || !visible.some((task) => task.completed);
    for (const task of visible) {
      const row = document.createElement('li');
      row.dataset.testid = 'directory-task-row';
      for (const [field, value] of [
        ['task-title', task.title], ['project-name', task.project_name],
        ['task-completion', task.completed ? 'Completed' : 'Open'],
        ['task-priority', task.priority], ['task-due-date', task.due_date],
        ['task-notes', task.notes],
      ]) {
        const text = document.createElement('span');
        text.dataset.testid = `directory-${field}`;
        text.textContent = value;
        row.append(text);
      }
      const open = document.createElement('button');
      open.type = 'button';
      open.textContent = 'Open project';
      open.addEventListener('click', () => { window.location.href = `/projects/${task.project_id}`; });
      row.append(open);
      list.append(row);
    }
  }
  async function setVisibleCompletion(value) {
    if ((value ? complete : reopen).disabled) return;
    app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
    const filters = { completed: value, scope: scope.value, filter: completion.value,
      priority: priority.value, from: appliedFrom, through: appliedThrough, query };
    loading = true;
    draw();
    try {
      tasks = await request('/api/task-directory/completion', {
        method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(filters),
      });
      resolved = true;
    } catch (error) { showError(error); }
    finally { loading = false; draw(); }
  }
  complete.addEventListener('click', () => setVisibleCompletion(true));
  reopen.addEventListener('click', () => setVisibleCompletion(false));
  for (const select of [scope, completion, priority]) select.addEventListener('change', draw);
  app.querySelector('#directory-search-form').addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    query = search.value.trim();
    search.value = query;
    draw();
  });
  app.querySelector('#due-range').addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
    const start = from.value.trim();
    const end = through.value.trim();
    if (!validRangeDate(start) || !validRangeDate(end)) {
      return showError(new Error('Due range must use valid YYYY-MM-DD dates'));
    }
    if (start && end && start > end) {
      return showError(new Error('Due from must not be after Due through'));
    }
    appliedFrom = start;
    appliedThrough = end;
    from.value = start;
    through.value = end;
    draw();
  });
  draw();
  try {
    tasks = await request('/api/task-directory');
    resolved = true;
  } catch (error) { showError(error); }
  finally { loading = false; draw(); }
}

function appendProject(project, onArchive) {
  const row = document.createElement('li');
  row.dataset.testid = 'project-row';
  const name = document.createElement('span');
  name.textContent = project.name;
  const button = document.createElement('button');
  button.type = 'button';
  button.textContent = 'Open project';
  button.addEventListener('click', () => { window.location.href = `/projects/${project.id}`; });
  const summary = document.createElement('span');
  summary.dataset.testid = 'project-summary';
  summary.textContent = `${project.completed}/${project.total} completed`;
  const archive = document.createElement('button');
  archive.type = 'button';
  archive.textContent = project.archived ? 'Restore project' : 'Archive project';
  archive.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
    archive.disabled = true;
    try {
      const saved = await request(`/api/projects/${project.id}`, {
        method: 'PATCH', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ archived: !project.archived }),
      });
      Object.assign(project, saved);
      onArchive();
    } catch (error) { archive.disabled = false; showError(error); }
  });
  row.append(name, summary, button, archive);
  app.querySelector('#projects').append(row);
  app.querySelector('#empty').hidden = true;
}

function renderRename(project) {
  const form = document.createElement('form');
  form.innerHTML = `
    <label for="new-project-name">New project name</label>
    <div class="create-controls">
      <input id="new-project-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="off">
      <button type="submit">Rename project</button>
    </div>`;
  const input = form.querySelector('input');
  const submit = form.querySelector('button');
  input.disabled = project.archived;
  submit.disabled = project.archived;
  form.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    if (submit.disabled) return;
    app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
    if (!input.value.trim()) return showError(new Error('Project name is required'));
    submit.disabled = true;
    try {
      const saved = await request(`/api/projects/${project.id}`, {
        method: 'PATCH', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ name: input.value }),
      });
      Object.assign(project, saved);
      app.querySelector('h1').textContent = project.name;
      document.title = `${project.name} · Workboard`;
      input.value = '';
      input.focus();
    } catch (error) { showError(error); }
    finally { submit.disabled = project.archived; }
  });
  app.append(form);
}

function renderDefaultPriority(project) {
  const controls = document.createElement('div');
  controls.innerHTML = `
    <label for="default-task-priority">Default task priority</label>
    <select id="default-task-priority">
      <option value="Low">Low</option>
      <option value="Normal">Normal</option>
      <option value="High">High</option>
    </select>`;
  const select = controls.querySelector('select');
  select.value = project.default_priority;
  select.disabled = project.archived;
  select.addEventListener('change', async () => {
    if (select.disabled) return;
    app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
    select.disabled = true;
    try {
      const saved = await request(`/api/projects/${project.id}`, {
        method: 'PATCH', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ default_priority: select.value }),
      });
      Object.assign(project, saved);
    } catch (error) { showError(error); }
    finally {
      select.value = project.default_priority;
      select.disabled = project.archived;
    }
  });
  app.append(controls);
}

async function renderTasks(project) {
  const projectId = project.id;
  const section = document.createElement('section');
  section.innerHTML = `
    <form>
      <label for="task-title">Task title</label>
      <div class="create-controls">
        <input id="task-title" name="title" type="text" autocomplete="off">
        <button type="submit" disabled>Create task</button>
      </div>
    </form>
    <h2>Tasks</h2>
    <form id="task-search-form">
      <label for="task-search">Task search</label>
      <input id="task-search" type="text" autocomplete="off">
      <button type="submit">Search tasks</button>
    </form>
    <label for="task-filter">Task filter</label>
    <select id="task-filter">
      <option value="all">All</option>
      <option value="open">Open</option>
      <option value="completed">Completed</option>
      <option value="deleted">Deleted</option>
    </select>
    <label for="priority-filter">Priority filter</label>
    <select id="priority-filter">
      <option value="all">All</option>
      <option value="Low">Low</option>
      <option value="Normal">Normal</option>
      <option value="High">High</option>
    </select>
    <form id="due-range">
      <label for="due-from">Due from</label>
      <input id="due-from" type="text" autocomplete="off">
      <label for="due-through">Due through</label>
      <input id="due-through" type="text" autocomplete="off">
      <button type="submit">Apply due range</button>
    </form>
    <p id="empty-tasks">No tasks to show.</p>
    <ul id="tasks" aria-label="Tasks"></ul>`;
  app.append(section);
  const form = section.querySelector('form');
  const input = section.querySelector('input');
  const submit = form.querySelector('button');
  const filter = section.querySelector('#task-filter');
  const priorityFilter = section.querySelector('#priority-filter');
  const rangeForm = section.querySelector('#due-range');
  const dueFrom = section.querySelector('#due-from');
  const dueThrough = section.querySelector('#due-through');
  const searchForm = section.querySelector('#task-search-form');
  const searchInput = section.querySelector('#task-search');
  let appliedQuery = '';
  let appliedFrom = '';
  let appliedThrough = '';
  const list = section.querySelector('ul');
  const endpoint = `/api/projects/${projectId}/tasks`;
  let tasks = [];
  let destinations = [];

  function drawTasks() {
    list.replaceChildren();
    const visible = tasks.filter((task) => matchesTask(task, filter.value,
      priorityFilter.value, appliedFrom, appliedThrough, appliedQuery));
    section.querySelector('#empty-tasks').hidden = visible.length > 0;
    for (const task of visible) {
      const readOnly = project.archived || Boolean(task.deleted);
      const row = document.createElement('li');
      row.dataset.testid = 'task-row';
      const title = document.createElement('span');
      title.textContent = task.title;
      const checkbox = document.createElement('input');
      checkbox.type = 'checkbox';
      checkbox.checked = task.completed;
      checkbox.disabled = readOnly;
      checkbox.setAttribute('aria-label', `Complete ${task.title}`);
      checkbox.addEventListener('change', async () => {
        if (checkbox.disabled) return;
        app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
        checkbox.disabled = true;
        try {
          const saved = await request(`${endpoint}/${task.id}`, {
            method: 'PATCH',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ completed: checkbox.checked }),
          });
          Object.assign(task, saved);
          drawTasks();
        } catch (error) {
          checkbox.checked = task.completed;
          checkbox.disabled = readOnly;
          showError(error);
        }
      });
      const renameForm = document.createElement('form');
      const renameLabel = document.createElement('label');
      renameLabel.htmlFor = `new-task-title-${task.id}`;
      renameLabel.textContent = 'New task title';
      const renameControls = document.createElement('div');
      renameControls.className = 'create-controls';
      const renameInput = document.createElement('input');
      renameInput.id = renameLabel.htmlFor;
      renameInput.type = 'text';
      renameInput.name = 'title';
      renameInput.autocomplete = 'off';
      renameInput.disabled = readOnly;
      const renameButton = document.createElement('button');
      renameButton.type = 'submit';
      renameButton.textContent = 'Rename task';
      renameButton.disabled = readOnly;
      renameForm.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        if (renameButton.disabled) return;
        app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
        if (!renameInput.value.trim()) return showError(new Error('Task title is required'));
        renameButton.disabled = true;
        try {
          const saved = await request(`${endpoint}/${task.id}`, {
            method: 'PATCH', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ title: renameInput.value }),
          });
          Object.assign(task, saved);
          title.textContent = task.title;
          checkbox.setAttribute('aria-label', `Complete ${task.title}`);
          renameInput.value = '';
          renameInput.focus();
          drawTasks();
        } catch (error) { showError(error); }
        finally { renameButton.disabled = readOnly; }
      });
      renameControls.append(renameInput, renameButton);
      renameForm.append(renameLabel, renameControls);
      const priorityControls = document.createElement('div');
      const priorityLabel = document.createElement('label');
      priorityLabel.htmlFor = `task-priority-${task.id}`;
      priorityLabel.textContent = 'Task priority';
      const priority = document.createElement('select');
      priority.id = priorityLabel.htmlFor;
      for (const value of ['Low', 'Normal', 'High']) {
        const option = document.createElement('option');
        option.value = value;
        option.textContent = value;
        priority.append(option);
      }
      priority.value = task.priority;
      priority.disabled = readOnly;
      priority.addEventListener('change', async () => {
        if (priority.disabled) return;
        app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
        priority.disabled = true;
        try {
          const saved = await request(`${endpoint}/${task.id}`, {
            method: 'PATCH', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ priority: priority.value }),
          });
          Object.assign(task, saved);
          drawTasks();
        } catch (error) { showError(error); }
        finally {
          priority.value = task.priority;
          priority.disabled = readOnly;
        }
      });
      priorityControls.append(priorityLabel, priority);
      const dueForm = document.createElement('form');
      const dueLabel = document.createElement('label');
      dueLabel.htmlFor = `task-due-date-${task.id}`;
      dueLabel.textContent = 'Task due date';
      const dueControls = document.createElement('div');
      dueControls.className = 'create-controls';
      const dueInput = document.createElement('input');
      dueInput.id = dueLabel.htmlFor;
      dueInput.type = 'text';
      dueInput.name = 'due_date';
      dueInput.autocomplete = 'off';
      dueInput.value = task.due_date;
      dueInput.disabled = readOnly;
      const dueButton = document.createElement('button');
      dueButton.type = 'submit';
      dueButton.textContent = 'Save due date';
      dueButton.disabled = readOnly;
      dueForm.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        if (dueButton.disabled) return;
        app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
        dueButton.disabled = true;
        try {
          const saved = await request(`${endpoint}/${task.id}`, {
            method: 'PATCH', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ due_date: dueInput.value }),
          });
          Object.assign(task, saved);
          dueInput.value = task.due_date;
          drawTasks();
        } catch (error) { showError(error); }
        finally { dueButton.disabled = readOnly; }
      });
      dueControls.append(dueInput, dueButton);
      dueForm.append(dueLabel, dueControls);
      const moveForm = document.createElement('form');
      const destinationLabel = document.createElement('label');
      destinationLabel.htmlFor = `destination-project-${task.id}`;
      destinationLabel.textContent = 'Destination project';
      const destinationSelect = document.createElement('select');
      destinationSelect.id = destinationLabel.htmlFor;
      for (const destination of destinations) {
        const option = document.createElement('option');
        option.value = String(destination.id);
        option.textContent = destination.name;
        destinationSelect.append(option);
      }
      const moveButton = document.createElement('button');
      moveButton.type = 'submit';
      moveButton.textContent = 'Move task';
      destinationSelect.disabled = readOnly || destinations.length === 0;
      moveButton.disabled = destinationSelect.disabled;
      moveForm.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        if (moveButton.disabled) return;
        app.querySelector('[role="alert"]')?.remove();
        moveButton.disabled = true;
        destinationSelect.disabled = true;
        try {
          await request(`${endpoint}/${task.id}`, {
            method: 'PATCH', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
